  "problem": "Which of the following diagrams shows all the $5$th roots of unity?",
  "worked_solution": "Geometrically, the $5$th roots of unity have the following properties:\n\n- all of them lie on the unit circle centered in the origin,\n\n- one of the roots is $1,$ corresponding to the point $(1,0)$ on the complex plane,\n\n- the roots form a regular pentagon (regular $5$-sided polygon).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is the following:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980994/assets/bf2edb811442fc770f6f3c119c06bca3c17d30537f1941448ddb6ab0afa3eb8a.png)",
